\fs14\
\b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the mode that should be used to break lines when laying out the paragraph\'27s text. This is one of:\
\fs14\
\pard \s65 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9553 \f0 \b \fs28 Value\tab Meaning\
\fs6\
\pard \s62 \li6753 \fi-4838 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9553 \f1 \b0 \fs28 NSLineBreakByWordWrapping\tab Wrapping occurs at word boundaries, unless the word itself doesn\'27t fit on a single line.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSLineBreakByCharWrapping\tab Wrapping occurs before the first character that doesn\'27t fit.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSLineBreakByClipping\tab Lines are simply not drawn past the edge of the text container.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSLineBreakByTruncatingHead\tab Each line is displayed so that the end fits in the container and the missing text is indicated by some kind of ellipsis glyph.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSLineBreakByTruncatingTail\tab Each line is displayed so that the beginning fits in the container and the missing text is indicated by some kind of ellipsis glyph.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSLineBreakByTruncatingMiddle\tab Each line is displayed so that the beginning and end fit in the container and the missing text is indicated by some kind of ellipsis glyph in the middle.\
\fs14\
\pard \s58 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b setLineBreakMode:\b0 \'80(NSMutableParagraphStyle)\
