\b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the distance in points from the margin of a text container to the end of lines. If positive, this is the distance from the leading margin (for example, the left margin in left-to-right text). If zero or negative, it\'27s the distance from the trailing margin.\
\fs14\
\fs28 For example, a paragraph style designed to fit exactly in a 2-inch wide container has a head indent of 0.0 and a tail indent of 0.0. One designed to fit with a quarter-inch margin has a head indent of 0.25 and a tail indent of \f3 -\f1 0.25.\
